  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BR Capacity Building for Management of Public Infrastructure Projects in Fed. Govt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project objective is to enhance the Brazilian Federal Government&apos;s capacity to appraise, execute, monitor and evaluate public sector investments systematically and to incorporate their results into policy making. Weak institutional capacity for appraisal and evaluation of public investment projects constitutes a serious obstacle to the efficiency of these investments, and to sustainable and inclusive economic growth under tight fiscal conditions in Brazil. The proposed activities will support: i) the definition of an institutional arrangement between the central ministries (Finance and Planning) and the infrastructure ministries for the process of  selection and evaluation of public investment projects, ii) the creation of critical mass in both ministries for the utilization of modern techniques of appraisal and evaluation of public investment projects through capacity building activities at the Finance and Planning ministries and iii) the establishment of an arrangement with a government training institution for the delivery of regular courses on project appraisal and evaluation to make sustainable the gains obtained in the (ii) guaranteeing the dissemination of the methodologies to the rest of Brazilian government, in particular the infrastructure ministries staff.</narrative>
  </description>
